==== an integer literal
42
----
(num "42")

==== a decimal point is not valid outside a string -- confirmed live, both engines
1.5
----
ERROR line 1 column 2

==== a string literal, quotes stripped in the s-expression only
"abc"
----
(str "abc")

==== percent escapes stay verbatim
"a%22b"
----
(str "a%22b")

==== a string may span lines
"a
b"
----
(str "a
b")

==== it is a distinguished operand
it
----
it

==== it is case-insensitive
IT
----
it

==== parens group without a node
(42)
----
(num "42")

==== nested parens still group without a node
((42))
----
(num "42")

==== a comment is trivia around an expression
/* pre */ 42 /* post */
----
(num "42")

==== an unterminated string is an error at the quote
("abc
----
ERROR line 1 column 2

==== empty parens are an error at the closing paren
()
----
ERROR line 1 column 2

==== an unclosed paren is an error at end of input
(1
----
ERROR line 1 column 3

==== trailing input after a complete expression
1 2
----
ERROR line 1 column 3
